  "2026-08-17T18:40:35.604Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: added scripts/release/command-grammar-gate.mjs, registered it in quality:static and the governed gate registry, updated release-contract acceptance, contract snapshots, token baselines, and CLI-refusal inventory after retiring ambiguous_list_all. Gate reports 129 commands, 129 destinations, 7 hidden deprecated aliases, 69 visible roots, and zero findings. Security scan, pnpm audit, package artifact, changelog check, lint, typecheck, and exact coverage pass."
  "2026-08-17T18:41:53.614Z","harness:codex","Closeout evidence: pm-changelog registry latest and installed versions are both 2026.8.17; generation added all five closed items and the subsequent --check reported unchanged."
  "2026-08-17T18:57:03.407Z","harness:codex","Preflight token evidence: canonical item-not-found recovery grows 3 tokens because the deprecated list-open spelling is replaced by pm list --status open --limit 20, while regenerated real-transport ceilings reduce small-workspace 626->552, large-workspace 1231->1055, returning-agent 597->371, and composite 2651->2178. The executable negative control still detects a seeded regression."
  "2026-08-17T19:03:53.473Z","harness:codex","GitHub governance evidence (2026-08-17): live gh inventory found 0 open PRs; 498 total issues (17 open, 481 closed), all 498 with a comment containing a corresponding PM item .toon link and no issue exceeding the 100-comment retrieval bound; 0 open Dependabot alerts; 0 open code-scanning alerts; 0 open secret-scanning alerts. pnpm audit reports no known vulnerabilities."
  "2026-08-17T19:04:56.635Z","harness:codex","GitHub governance evidence (2026-08-17): live gh inventory found 0 open PRs; 498 total issues (17 open, 481 closed), all 498 with a comment containing a corresponding PM item .toon link and no issue exceeding the 100-comment retrieval bound; 0 open Dependabot alerts; 0 open code-scanning alerts; 0 open secret-scanning alerts. pnpm audit reports no known vulnerabilities. Registry outdated inventory has only two incompatible majors, each retained under its existing unclaimed canonical PM owner (pm-ksr40d and pm-do5b); no duplicate item was created."
  "2026-08-17T19:36:32.688Z","harness:codex","Final pre-commit verification evidence: pnpm verify:preflight passed build/typecheck, repository static and context assurance, package boundary, SDK parity, surface replication, 129-row command grammar, tracker context, gate registry, SDK import/CLI transport floors, graph composition, record integrity, token surface, 518 files / 7,521 tests at exact 100/100/100/100, version sync, secrets, packed npx smoke, 88-command package-first dogfood, and live Sentry/telemetry (critical=0 high=0). The terminal Greptile gate refused only because there was no committed diff yet, as designed; rerun follows on the commit."
  "2026-08-17T20:45:38.018Z","harness:codex","PR #1058 review-correction evidence: the grammar census now separates 114 always-present core commands from conditional package-owned destinations while retaining a 131-row declared universe; the active repository has 129 commands and 61 non-package visible roots. The mandatory gate also verifies 87 discoverable MCP actions against 31 tools, 29 narrow action bindings, and the documented pm_mutate composite waiver, with negative controls for duplicate, missing, stale, undiscoverable, unbound, and stale-waiver cases. Empty-tracker and active-package executions both report zero findings."
  "2026-08-17T20:45:40.400Z","harness:codex","Final verification after review fixes: 518/518 test files and 7,525/7,525 tests pass with exact coverage statements 54,871/54,871, branches 40,928/40,928, functions 11,296/11,296, and lines 52,962/52,962. pnpm quality:static, contracts:check, CLI transport floor, package artifact, 88-command package-first dogfood, secret scan, pnpm audit, diff check, and focused 133-test SDK/grammar rerun all pass."
  "2026-08-17T21:20:53.390Z","harness:codex","Final CodeRabbit round evidence: hidden aliases are defensively excluded from the visible-surface metric, the redundant split was removed, keep-as-is remains public-compatible but now fails closed without a reason, the census is injected in tests instead of mutating exported state, and the gate test restores stdout/process exit state after every case. Focused 152-test validation, contracts check, SDK surface check, full 7,525-test exact coverage, and mandatory static quality all pass."
  "2026-08-17T21:44:27.463Z","harness:codex","CI evidence: PR #1058 exact head 82834bfc4 failed Gates (static) because clean ESLint measured verifyPmCliGrammar cognitive complexity 20 versus the mandatory limit 16. The earlier local pass was cache-masked; correction will be validated with cache disabled and the focused/full mandatory gates."
  "2026-08-17T21:55:54.235Z","harness:codex","Exact-head correction evidence: rewrote destination validation as a declarative flatMap/reduce pipeline, preserving all missing, duplicate, keep-as-is reason, and unknown-noun diagnostics while reducing clean ESLint cognitive complexity below the mandatory threshold. Cache-disabled ESLint, typecheck, 10 focused grammar/gate tests, the full static contract/graph/security suite through its independent gates, isolated SDK import-cost benchmark, and 518 files / 7,525 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 all pass."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T07:13:37.719Z","harness:claude-code","Surface-growth measurement for the conformance gate this item defines (2026-07-25): pm --help now lists 78 top-level commands in this repo (76 in the isolated fixture the token-budget gate measures) across 109 lines. pm-n7rr's charter was written against roughly 60 and targets roughly 15 nouns, so the surface has grown by about a third while the consolidation epic has been open. The 78 include all eight list-* status variants, four history-* commands, three completion-* data providers, three lifecycle aliases (start-task, pause-task, close-task), three calendar shortcuts (meet, event, remind), and package-registered commands (beads, changelog, dedupe-audit, dedupe-merge, comments-audit, normalize, item, pm). This is the concrete baseline the grammar gate has to freeze: without it the count has no ceiling, and every new command adds to the 49,872-token full help surface agents pay to discover the tool."
  "2026-07-26T10:50:05.718Z","harness:claude-code","Prerequisite discovered 2026-07-26: the twelve-noun target table on pm-n7rr has no placement for five live CORE nouns — graph, merge, events, copy, normalize — three of which (graph, merge, events) shipped after the table was authored. A conformance gate built against the current table would reject shipped functionality. Sequence the placement decision (recorded on pm-n7rr, ruled by ADR pm-pbyu) before the allowlist is declared as data, otherwise the allowlist encodes the omission."
  "2026-07-26T22:10:53.688Z","harness:claude-code","Why the ratchet belongs here and not on the ADR, recorded 2026-07-27.\n\nThis item exists to stop the surface regrowing after consolidation. Measured today the surface is growing before consolidation, at roughly 1.3 top-level spellings per day since the grammar ADR was written — the series is on pm-pbyu. The gate this item will build is the same mechanism in both cases: compare the live surface against a declared expectation and fail when it drifts. The only difference is what the expectation is. After the noun table is accepted the expectation is the table. Before it is accepted the expectation can simply be the current count.\n\nThat distinction matters because it makes a useful half of this item shippable now. A count baseline needs no grammar decision, no alias shim, and no migration; it needs a committed number, a check that reads the live surface, and a documented waiver path. It also produces the first honest measurement of intent: every waiver is a recorded decision to grow the surface, which is exactly the evidence the ADR is missing.\n\nSequencing is unchanged. The full conformance gate still waits on pm-pbyu and on the placement disposition recorded as pm-n7rr note 13. The ratchet is the tranche of this item that does not."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-17T21:55:55.108Z","harness:codex","CI parity lesson: incremental ESLint cache results are insufficient closeout evidence after late review edits. Run the edited file with --no-cache before push; clean CI correctly exposed cognitive complexity that an earlier cached local aggregate did not."
